@startuml billing-credential-desktop-vs-hosted
' ============================================================================
'  WHO PAYS, AND WHO GETS STOPPED - the model-call credential across the three
'  modes (desktop BYOK, desktop Cloud, hosted web), the asymmetry that leaves
'  hosted users metered-but-never-stopped, and the one-rule fix.
'  STATUS: BUILT (uncommitted) - turn_key now prefers the caller's own session
'  token; accounts publishes `credits_enforced` so a zero balance means
'  EXHAUSTED only for accounts that were granted credits (no lockout of the
'  existing free tier); MODEL_PROXY_REQUIRE_CREDITS=1 closes it deployment-wide.
'  Pinned by tests/unit/test_model_access.py + tests/unit/test_metering.py.
'  Same conventions as tenant-isolation-current-and-fix.puml and
'  agent-authoring-current-and-fix.puml.
'
'  THE BREAK, one sentence:
'    TWO places answer "which account is this call for" - the pre-call GATE
'    reads `user_api_key_dict.user_id`, the post-call BILLING reads that OR
'    the OpenAI `user` field - and the hosted daemon fills in only the second,
'    so its users are charged correctly and refused never.
'
'  WHY THE FIX IS NOT "teach the gate to also read `user`": that adds a SECOND
'  way to identify an account, and the two would drift the first time either
'  changes. The credential itself already carries the identity everywhere
'  except one branch - so fix the branch, not the reader:
'
'    pay with the CALLER'S OWN credential whenever the caller has one
'    the deployment's master key only where there is genuinely no caller
'
'  Then hosted authenticates exactly as desktop Cloud does, `user_id` is set
'  by construction, and the gate fires without learning anything new.
'
'  Render (from this folder):
'    java -jar ../../../plantuml.jar -tpng billing-credential-desktop-vs-hosted.puml
' ============================================================================

skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam ArrowFontColor #444444
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #6A6A6A
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF4E5
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #C9A227
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF8DC
skinparam NoteBorderColor #C9B458
skinparam partitionBorderColor #9AA0B5
skinparam partitionFontStyle bold
skinparam partitionFontSize 13

title Model-call billing - desktop vs hosted, the enforcement gap, and the one-rule fix\nthe CREDENTIAL is what tells the proxy whose call this is; hosted is the one mode that pays with\nsomebody else's - so it bills the right account and can never refuse it

start

partition "0 . ONE FUNNEL, ONE DECISION   (DAEMON, every mode)" #E8F0FE {
  :every model call a tool or the loop makes goes through the funnel
  (infrastructure/llm/oneshot.py) into **model_proxy.apply()** - it
  retargets the call at OUR proxy and attaches a credential;
  :**turn_key()** is the whole decision, per CONNECTION rather than per
  process: local-billing pays nothing, a deployment that FORCED the proxy
  on (env url / config enabled) pays with its master key, everyone else
  pays with the connection's own session token
  (infrastructure/llm/model_proxy.py turn_key + configure);
}

switch (turn_key: what does THIS turn pay with?)

case ( "" - desktop LOCAL / BYOK )

  partition "1 . DESKTOP LOCAL - the user's own provider key" #E6F4EA {
    :billing mode is `local`, so no proxy credential and no retarget:
    the call goes DIRECT to the provider on the user's own key;
    :nothing to gate. The user is the payer and the provider bills
    them - our credits never enter the picture;
  }

case ( the connection's SESSION TOKEN - desktop CLOUD )

  partition "2 . DESKTOP CLOUD - the caller pays as themselves   (WORKS)" #E6F4EA {
    :not forced, but the signed-in connection HAS a session, so
    `enabled()` is true for this turn and the session token is the
    credential;
    :**proxy auth** resolves that token against Accounts and returns
    `UserAPIKeyAuth(api_key=..., user_id=<account>)`
    (model_proxy/custom_auth.py, the session branch);
    :**PRE-CALL GATE** reads `user_id`, finds the account, asks
    Accounts for its funding view, and refuses BEFORE any money moves:
    not entitled to this agent -> 403, no credits left -> 402;
    :**POST-CALL** debits the same account (metadata user_api_key_user_id)
    and records cost, tokens and margin;
  }

case ( the deployment's MASTER KEY - hosted WEB )

  partition "3 . HOSTED WEB - the SERVER pays, the user is only named   (BROKEN)" #FDECEA {
    :the env proxy url makes the deployment FORCED, so every turn pays
    with `AGENTD_MODEL_PROXY_KEY` - the server's own credential - no
    matter which signed-in human triggered it;
    :the account does travel, but in a DIFFERENT place: apply() writes
    it into the OpenAI **`user`** field, because the credential itself
    no longer says who this is for;
    :**proxy auth** matches the master key and returns
    `UserAPIKeyAuth(api_key=...)` with **NO user_id** - by design, the
    branch was written when only ops used that key;
    if (pre-call gate: is there a user_id?) then (no - every hosted turn)
      :**returns None = ALLOW.** The comment reads "master-key
      infra / ops calls carry no account to meter" - true when it was
      written, false the day the hosted daemon became a master-key
      caller that DOES carry an account;
      :=> entitlement and credit checks NEVER RUN for hosted users;
    else (yes - never happens here)
      :the 402 / 403 refusals fire as designed;
    endif
    :**POST-CALL** still finds the account, because billing reads
    `user_api_key_user_id` **OR the `user` field** - so the ledger is
    debited correctly;
    :=> THE ASYMMETRY: charged accurately, refused never. A hosted
    account at zero credits, or with no subscription to a paid agent,
    keeps generating - and the overspend is only ever visible after
    the money is gone;
  }

endswitch

partition "4 . THE ROOT CAUSE - two readers of one fact" #FDECEA {
  :"which account is this call for" is answered TWICE, from different
  fields: the GATE reads `user_id` only, BILLING reads `user_id` or
  `user`. Hosted fills in only the second;
  :teaching the gate to also read `user` would close the hole and
  leave the real defect standing - two identity paths that must be
  kept in step by whoever edits either one next;
}

partition "5 . THE FIX - the caller pays with the caller's credential" #E6F4EA {
  :**one line of policy, in turn_key()**: when this turn has a session
  token, PAY WITH IT; fall back to the deployment's master key only
  when there is genuinely no caller credential;
  :hosted then authenticates EXACTLY as desktop Cloud does - the proxy
  resolves the token, sets `user_id`, and the pre-call gate fires **by
  construction**. No new field, no second identity path, no `if hosted`;
  :the master key keeps the calls it was actually written for - cron
  ticks, public/anonymous app visitors, system work like auto-titling -
  which is precisely the "no account to meter" branch. The comment
  becomes TRUE again instead of quietly wrong;
  :the `user` field stays as belt-and-braces attribution for those
  account-less-but-attributable calls. Nothing is removed;
}

partition "6 . WHAT EACH MODE FEELS AFTER   (same code, different values)" #E0F2F1 {
  :**desktop LOCAL** - unchanged, byte for byte: no proxy credential,
  no gate, the user's own provider key pays;
  :**desktop CLOUD** - unchanged: it already paid with the session
  token, which is now simply the general rule rather than the
  fall-through case;
  :**hosted WEB** - refusals start working: 402 at zero credits, 403
  without entitlement, checked before the spend instead of after;
}

stop

note right
  ==== THIS IS NOT THE FALLBACK CHAIN THE CODE WARNS ABOUT ====
  turn_key's own docstring refuses to chain "on emptiness",
  and it is right: the bug it prevents is a STALE SERVER KEY
  silently deciding who gets billed when no session is present.
  The fix chains the other way - the CALLER'S credential first,
  the server's only when no caller exists - so the failure mode
  it guards against cannot occur: we never bill a person on a
  credential that is not theirs.

  ==== PRECONDITION, DECIDE BEFORE SHIPPING ====
  Enforcement that has never run will start refusing the moment
  it does. If signup grants no credits, EVERY hosted call 402s
  on the first turn. Wire the signup grant / default budget in
  the same change, not after it.

  ==== KNOWN RESIDUE (unchanged by this fix) ====
  * hosted CRON pins only `{account_id}` - no session token to
    re-resolve, so those turns keep the master key and stay
    ungated. The code already says so; re-resolve a token there
    before offering hosted autonomy.
  * PUBLIC / anonymous app visitors have no account at all:
    spend is recorded as unbilled_cost_usd, bounded only by the
    connection and concurrency caps.
  * tools.invoke never calls start_usage, so the DAEMON-side
    per-turn accumulator reads zero for direct tool runs. The
    proxy still debits them; only the local view is blind.
end note

legend left
  | Piece | desktop LOCAL | desktop CLOUD | hosted WEB today | hosted after the fix |
  | credential (turn_key) | none - direct to provider | the connection's session token | the deployment's MASTER KEY | the connection's session token |
  | account known to proxy auth | n/a | yes - `user_id` from the token | NO - master key carries none | yes - `user_id` from the token |
  | account named elsewhere | n/a | n/a | yes - the OpenAI `user` field | same, as belt-and-braces |
  | pre-call gate (402 / 403) | n/a - user pays provider | FIRES | SKIPPED - the hole | FIRES |
  | post-call ledger debit | n/a | correct | correct | correct |
  | net effect | user's own money | metered and enforced | metered, never enforced | metered and enforced |
endlegend

@enduml
